s and account reconciliations. Organize, file and maintain financial documents (invoices, receipts, vouchers). Assist with audit requests by compiling supporting documentation. Ensure compliance with internal controls, financial policies and confidentiality requirements. Carry out additional duties and ad-hoc finance projects as assigned by Head of Finance. Who you are Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Economics or related discipline. Current participant in the national service program (available for the full service period) Basic knowledge of accounting principles and bookkeeping. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel (formulas, filtering, basic pivot tables). Familiarity with accounting software ( Sage) is an advantage. Accurate data entry skills and strong numerical ability. Apply Now Apply Company About Contact Careers Learn Support Lodge a Complaint Whistleblower Portal Our Commitment To Professional Conduct Product Fido Credit Fido Score Credit Breakdown Business Loan Impact Report ESG Report Legals Referral Program T&Cs Legal Discounts Upsales T&C Terms of Service Referral Plan T&C Commitment to info sec. End User License Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Follow Us © All rights are reserved under Fido Microcredit, 2025 Ghana (English)",
